    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-ceiling plays: **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Gunnar Henderson** (68.29). **Jackson Merrill** is our strongest start, benefiting from a massive 19% boost due to a soft matchup against Kelly (xERA 5.37) and a favorable platoon edge, while **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s score is buoyed by a significant park factor (+16%) that outweighs the risk of facing the southpaw Peterson. While **Jacob Wilson** (66.46) and **Coby Mayo** (65.57) round out the top tier of our offense, both take advantage of that same favorable park environment against the Diamondbacks. We are specifically looking for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** to navigate the Peterson matchup carefully; while the park boost is helpful, the \"Elite Hold SP\" penalty highlights the difficulty of securing stolen bases today, putting extra pressure on their ability to generate runs via extra-base hits.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Sam Antonacci** (35.73), who fell just shy of our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor for starting consideration. Despite a decent base projection, his score was cratered by a brutal matchup against the elite xERA (2.08) of Sandoval and a detrimental L/L platoon disadvantage. Ultimately, **Dominic Smith** (57.09) earned the nod over the bench options due to his stable platoon edge and a manageable matchup against Keller. We must remain cautious with **Liam Hicks** (40.73) and **Miguel Vargas** (42.64); both are flirting with our bench threshold as they square off against premier arms Miller and Sandoval, respectively. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined on the IL, we are effectively playing a man down in terms of elite speed, making the efficiency of **Brayan Rocchio** (59.19) and **Heliot Ramos** (62.07) vital to keeping our SB category production afloat. Keep a close eye on the weather and late lineup changes, as the margin for error is razor-thin when facing pitching staffs with sub-3.00 xERAs.",
